Subject: [PATCH] Type the approval-required error; annotate audit; add MkDocs
 skeleton

- core: add ApprovalRequired(PolicyViolation). ToolRuntime and the app
  capability registry now classify a refusal by exception type instead of
  searching the message for "approval", which mislabelled a denied tool
  whose name contained that word. Regression test added; it fails on the
  previous behaviour.
- PRODUCTION_AUDIT.md: add a status block. Re-checked each finding against
  current code by reading it: 7 fixed, 1 mitigated, 2 open (DRACO-003,
  DRACO-010). Original reproductions were not re-run.
- docs: add mkdocs.yml and docs/index.md over the existing pages. Builds with
  --strict. HISTORY_PURGE.md and the stale PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md are excluded.
- pyproject: add a `docs` extra; .gitignore: ignore site/.

